{
  "$comment": "Catalog of media generation models (AI Studio spec §7.2). ONE source for the route (zod), SQL (ai_models, seeded in migrations — check:api compares the two) and the worker. `limits.maxReferences`: how many reference images the model takes (0 = none; the prompt box does not attach the selected image). `price.unit`: generation = per generation; second = per second (rounded up); kchars = per 1,000 prompt characters (rounded up); explainer = `credits` per started 10 s plus `voiceKchars` per started 1,000 characters of narration (the beats' `say`, trimmed, joined with one space). Models with `provider: fake` run only with OPENCMO_AI_FAKE=1 outside production. `providerModel`: the provider's model id — read by the worker; env `OPENCMO_AI_MODEL_<ID>` (e.g. OPENCMO_AI_MODEL_GEMINI_VIDEO) overrides it, so a real id can be pinned without editing the catalog. Gemini prices are PROVISIONAL (COSTS.md §6c). `limits.scene`: 3D Studio and explainers — the spec also has `scene` (SceneContentSchema in packages/clip-three/src/spec.ts, or the explainer script); `prompt` is only a summary for people. `elevenlabs-voice`: narration with per-word timings (captions for voiceovers); voice name → voice_id in the Python adapter; price PROVISIONAL (COSTS.md §6e). `motion-explainer` (docs/explainer-build.md): scene {template: \"explainer\", code_ref, title, beats, accent?} plus `voice` (a premade ElevenLabs voice) and `prompt` = \"Explainer: <title>\"; price PROVISIONAL until measured on Modal.",
